# Internal engineering docs — never part of the deployed site.
# QC-TRACKER.md was publicly served at zamborin.com/QC-TRACKER.md until 2026-08-24.
# Nothing at runtime fetches a .md; the only reference is a comment in shared/ads.js.
*.md

# Measuring harnesses — instruments, not the site. Kept in git because several
# of them found bugs nothing else could and they are how a change gets
# re-verified, but they are dev pages and have no business being served:
# tools/portal-build.mjs was already reachable at zamborin.com/tools/, the same
# way QC-TRACKER.md was. They run against the local dev server.
/tools/

# Per-game measuring harnesses, for the same reason as /tools/.
#
# BELT AND BRACES, not a live leak. Checked against production first, and the
# claim that prompted this was wrong: .mjs is not served by this deployment at
# all, so ballast/tune-m0.mjs, ballast/tune-play.mjs and ricochet/tune-gate.mjs
# already 404 while ballast/play.js beside them returns 200. This rule exists
# so that a harness written as .js one day does not quietly become a public
# page the way QC-TRACKER.md did.
#
# NOT shared/qc/doc-audit.js. That one is a harness too, and it is served on
# purpose: the documented way to run it is to fetch it FROM THE ORIGIN against
# the live site, so excluding it would break the audit rather than tidy it.
tune-*.mjs
tune-*.js
